From 6cac48ad5fb985f885000dd33acdaf3e8667602d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard DEMONGEOT <richard@rdem-systems.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:08:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] fork: build and release the Nimbus Backup brand in CI

Upstream's merge renamed every artifact in build-and-release.yml to
ProxmoxBackupClient and replaced the Nimbus release notes; the fork
keeps its own copy of the workflow (upstream only changed branding):

- restore the fork's workflow (NimbusBackup.exe/.msi artifacts, Nimbus
  release notes, VirusTotal/attestation on NimbusBackup*),
- stamp the Nimbus identity into gui/wails.json before `wails build`
  (upstream's is neutral), so the GUI exe is NimbusBackup.exe,
- build the MSI from NimbusBackup.wxs (legacy UpgradeCode),
- pin the Wails CLI to v2.13.0, matching the library upstream moved to,
- disable upstream's goreleaser release.yaml tag trigger so two
  workflows don't race to publish the same release.
---
 .github/workflows/build-and-release.yml | 119 ++++++++++++++----------
 .github/workflows/release.yaml          |  11 ++-
 2 files changed, 79 insertions(+), 51 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/build-and-release.yml b/.github/workflows/build-and-release.yml
index 48e5a6e..145a234 100644
